  "output": "Based on prior audits (memory shows this exact analysis was already run 3+ times on Jul 9-10), let me give a fresh, concrete pass on the code actually shown here rather than repeat generic findings.\n\n## N+1 query patterns\nNo DB code is visible in this snippet (that lives in `backend/`), but the frontend mirrors the anti-pattern: `src/utils/transcript.ts:buildConversationItems` runs `events.filter(...)` then `.map(...)` then a `.sort()` per render, called once per transcript view — fine at small scale, but if `TranscriptsView` calls this per-row for a list, it's effectively N+1 client-side work. Confirm it's only called for the single open transcript, not mapped across a list.\n\n## Unnecessary React re-renders\n- `src/hooks/useToasts.ts` — solid, already uses `useCallback`.\n- `src/hooks/useKeyboardShortcuts.ts` — good pattern (refs to avoid re-registering listeners).\n- Risk area not shown here but flagged previously: `CampaignsView` rebuilding `ruleByOutcome`/strategy objects every render — wrap in `useMemo` keyed on `campaign.dialing_strategy`.\n\n## Caching opportunities\n`src/utils/cache.ts` already provides a versioned localStorage cache (`cacheGet`/`cacheSet` + `pruneOldCache`). Good foundation — but nothing in the shown API layer (`src/api.ts`'s `request()`) uses it. Concrete suggestion:\n\n```ts\n// src/api.ts\nimport { cacheGet, cacheSet } from './utils/cache';\n\nexport async function cachedRequest<T>(path: string, ttlMs = 30_000): Promise<T> {\n  const cached = cacheGet<{ ts: number; data: T } | null>(path, null);\n  if (cached && Date.now() - cached.ts < ttlMs) return cached.data;\n  const data = await request<T>(path);\n  cacheSet(path, { ts: Date.now(), data });\n  return data;\n}\n```\nApply to rarely-changing endpoints: `phrases()`, `outcomes()`, `languageSettings()`, `platformSettings()`.\n\n## Memory leaks\n- `useToasts.ts:24` — `setTimeout(() => dismissToast(id), durationMs)` is never cleared on unmount. If the component using this hook unmounts before the toast expires, this fires a state update on an unmounted component. Fix:\n```ts\nconst showToast = useCallback((message: string, tone: ToastTone = 'success', durationMs = DEFAULT_DURATION_MS) => {\n  counterRef.current += 1;\n  const id = `toast-${counterRef.current}`;\n  setToasts((prev) => [...prev, { id, message, tone }]);\n  if (durationMs > 0) {\n    const timer = setTimeout(() => dismissToast(id), durationMs);\n    timersRef.current.push(timer); // clear in a cleanup effect at the consumer, or track+clearAll on unmount\n  }\n  return id;\n}, [dismissToast]);\n```\nSimplest robust fix: track timer ids in a ref array and clear them all in a `useEffect` cleanup.\n\n## Redundant computations\n- `src/utils/transcript.ts:buildConversationItems` recomputes `normalizeTranscriptRole`, `formatTime`, `timestampValue` for every turn on every call — fine if memoized by caller (`useMemo(() => buildConversationItems(transcript, events), [transcript, events])`), but if the parent view calls this inline in JSX without memoization, it recalculates on every keystroke/unrelated state change.\n- `src/utils/formatting.ts:parseApiDate` runs a regex test every call; called repeatedly (`formatDate`, `formatTime`, `timeAgo` all call it) — not a bottleneck at this scale, skip.\n\n## Priority\n1. Fix the `useToasts` timer leak (real bug, cheap fix).\n2. Memoize `buildConversationItems` call sites in transcript views.\n3. Wire `cacheGet`/`cacheSet` into rarely-changing GET endpoints in `api.ts`.\n\nNote: this exact audit (N+1/re-renders/caching/leaks) was already run and stored in project memory on Jul 9–10 with more backend-side findings (unbounded `find({})`, uncompiled regex in `fuzzy_match_opt_id`, analytics in-memory aggregation). Want me to pull those observations (`get_observations`) to check whether those fixes have since landed, rather than re-deriving them from this truncated snippet?\n",
